\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch Track Descriptions (copied from the posts on Random Lunacy and Tumblr): }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch  }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch 1) Trip 2 Hemel [On A Santa Ting Mix] }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch And today marks the official start of the very first 12 Tracks Of Christmas project! The idea is that every second/even numbered day, all the way up to Christmas Eve, I will release a brand new track. Some will be Christmas themed, some will (at least) be winter themed, others might just be general tracks, and Ill be doing them under any and all aliases I work under. There might even be a remix or cover here and there! }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch For the first track this year, I decided to finish up a song I started a couple of weeks ago. Its a fairly simple number that is an intentional homage to the classic rave (tune and one of my personal favourite records), Trip 2 Trumpton. I had originally wanted to sample a kids show of some kind to keep in line with the homage, but technical issues got in the way. At the very least, I managed to get the track intro done (and yes, that is me speaking, albeit under a hi-pass filter). This will probably wind up being the longest of the 12 tracks, but that all depends on how busy I wind up being over the next month. As for the relevance to Christmas/the deal with the name; Hemel Hempstead is the name of a city a few miles away from where I live, and is where me and my folks/uncle have done our Christmas shopping for the last 3 or 4 years. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch  }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch  }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch 2) Survive (Like I Know You Can)}{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch This one, admittedly, doesn't really have any relevance to Christmas, or the Christmas season per say. This piece of music in some ways could be considered to be what I think the mindset of someone that continues to be brave and face their demons, be they haunting memories of the past or even just the will to get up, might sound like- somewhere between happy and sad and yet both at the same time. ... Yeah, that sentence was in English I think. I drew inspiration from equal parts what I've seen in so many friends of mine, all of whom have their own demons to face, and my own experiences and battles with anxiety and depression (over the past year especially). The track was also inspired by the works of Underworld and Aphex Twin, the tracks Best Mamgu Ever and Flim. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch  }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch 3) The Most Deadly Game: Theme Of Guidestuck }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch Whoa now hold up, a FINISHED bit of Guidestuck music? And its a 12 Tracks Of Christmas entry too? Goddamn son call the media this shit\uc1\u8217\'92s bananas. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch So, around about the last week or so, I\uc1\u8217\'92ve been really getting into Guidestuck. Guidestuck is a Homestuck fan adventure created by one miss scarvenrot, and generally switches the rolls between the kids/guardians and trolls/lusii around in a complete 180. There is definitely a lot more to Guidestuck then that, but you didn\uc1\u8217\'92t come here for a plot synopsis! }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch There\uc1\u8217\'92s been a contest going on for a while, and while I have been working on a couple of pieces of Guidestuck music, Im kinda stuck on where to go with them. And after finishing Attract Mode last night and deciding to stick it on another project, I was kinda lost with what to do for today. Then somehow this happened and all my problems were solved! }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch This is, effectively, a general theme for Guidestuck rather then any character or land or scenario specifically. Like you could probably think of this as my interpretation of Guidestuck\uc1\u8217\'92s answer to Suburban Jungle. The piece as a whole is kind of a mish mash between synthpop, soundtrack, techno, drum n bass, and even a bit of (fake) chiptune at the very end for good measure. Im planning on doing a full chiptune mix using the little chiptune section at the end as well, so keep an eye out for that sometime in the near future! }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch Again, this track has no real relevance to Christmas, but I promise the next one will be! }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch  }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch 4) Snowfall In Shibuya (A Tribute To Nujabes)}{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch Track 4 of the 12 Tracks project, and it's a hip hop joint. Because to be frank I've needed to put out a Hip Hop track that actually sounds sorta pro-ish, and not just like a cheap beat thrown together by an amateur like most of my previous attempts. This is oldskool hip hop style; there ain't no overdone 808 booms and snaps here, just breaks, horns, and piano loops. Very, very, VERY heavily inspired by the jazzy vibes of Nujabes, a Japanese hip hop producer most known for providing music for the anime series Samurai Champloo, especially for the series' iconic theme song Battlecry (done in collaboration with rapper Shing02). Sadly, he was taken from us back in 2010, after he was involved in a serious car accident. He was only 36 years old. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch  }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch 5) The Bitter Battle Of Manor Road }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch The fifth entry in the 12 Tracks Of Christmas project, and its a bit of a strange one. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch Well, its not flat out weird, but it mixes elements of rave, breakbeat, acid, and ambient all together. In a lot of ways, its a little bit like a track made by The Freestylers, or a recent Shut Up & Dance tune, and probably wouldn\uc1\u8217\'92t be too out of place in a wipEout game. Which Im ok with, because Im a BIG fan of wipEout. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch As for the relevance to Christmas/the title, allow me to explain; about two or so years ago, it had snowed quite heavily very close to Christmas (most of it had melted by Christmas day, though), quite late in the day. I was hanging out with a few mates for most of the night, and we didn\uc1\u8217\'92t notice it had snowed, or how heavy it had snowed, until about 11Oclock at night. Upon this discovery, we did what any normal 18/19 year olds would do; we went out and had a grandiose Snowball Fight- no, a full out Snowball War that lasted until about 3 or 4 in the morning. We actually rang up a couple of other friends of ours and had them come all the way down to London Colney just for the fight, thats how serious this shit was to us. Most of the fight took place on a street near to where I live named Manor Road- hence, the title. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch  }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch 6) The Undersea Peanut & The Mean Beans Are On (Think)Tank! Patrol }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch I've been fascinated by the concepts of Mash Ups (the mixing of two or more songs together) and Mastermixes (the art of making a (usually long) track without a traditional verse-chorus-verse structure that usually seems more like multiple songs mixed together- or actually IS multiple songs mixed together), and partially due to not having enough time to make a longer, fuller track, I got my chance to attempt to realise that with what limited technology I currently have at my disposal. It's halfway between a (very short) Mastermix and a Mash Up and contains a large amount of original material, but it's a good start none the less. Hopefully the 14th's track will be a bit longer (permitting I don't have further technology problems and am not sick as shit on the 14th). Samples from The Goofy Goober Song, Dr. Robotnik's Mean Bean Machine, and Tank!}{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch  }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch 7) Coolkid [J-MACHine's '93 Style Remix] }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch The day's not even started and already I've done track 7 for the 12 Tracks project! }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch So basically IKARUS is a cool fucking dude that makes boss tunes the likes of wish I was only half as talented enough to make, and Coolkid is definitely one of my favourites (and to say Im humbled that a track of mine wound up as part of coloUrs & mayhem alongside it is a huge understatement). I\uc1\u8217\'92ve wanted to put my own spin on Coolkid for a while, but I wasn\uc1\u8217\'92t sure what sort of style I wanted to do it in- originally I thought of just doing something similar to Gold Mage in style under the repeatedScales name, but I thought that was a little bit too predictable. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch In the end, I settled on an Oldskool Hardcore/early 90s rave type sound, because I thought the main melody riff really worked when rendered with Raves synths. Many, many liberties are taken and a lot of original melodies/chord progressions are added, but most major parts from the original song are recreated by ear to the best of my ability. This was, however, partially done from memory, so it might not be 100% accurate. Still, I tried my best. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch 8) A Self Portrait in 64 Colours}{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch This track was originally written as a standalone song in November of 2014, just before production on Battlemania got underway. Due to the removal of the remix of Given A (and it\uc1\u8217\'92s bonus demo), it was selected to replace it as the 8th track on the album to round out the total count of 12 tracks.}{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch  }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch 9) Merry Glitchmas: My Best Friend The Arpeggiator Comes Over For Santa Day }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch The ninth track done for the 12 Tracks Of Christmas Project. Although not actually the first chronologically (or even the first composed), this is the first in a long planned series of tracks I've named the My Best Friend The Arpeggiator series, done solely under my Visor Jack alias. These songs typically won't be very long, will be fairly minimalistic-ish type guff, and as the name implies rely on heavy use of arpeggiated rhythms. A lot of my work uses arpeggiated rhythms and synth lines anyway, but I ramp it up to 11 on these tracks on purpose, because I love the kind of looped sound it gives off. If you're unsure of what 'arpeggiated rhythms' means or it's use in electronic music, I'd say look it up; trust me, there's a 100% chance you've heard it used in a song, as even pop songs have made heavy use of it (especially 80s pop). Nothing too complex about this one, it's just a short, sweet, mechanical sounding dance-type number to tap your feet along with. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch  }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch 10) Silenced Without A Trace [Theme of Clapham] }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch The tenth track done for the 12 Tracks project; we're in the home stretch now! }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch Todays piece is another gift track (all the remaining tracks will be) done for a friend of mine who I've been through some very weird and uneasy times with this year, but who is nonetheless important to me. They're not only creative, but incredibly talented at both writing and drawing, and one of their ideas struck such a chord with me, that it lead to inspiring this track. There's definitely some shades of inspiration from Akira Yamaoka's work on Silent Hill here too. Also, at 65bpm, it's probably the slowest track I've done. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch Stay ghetto, Terry. It's no pair of shoes, but I hope it impresses all the same. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch  }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch 11) Emergency On Old Mother Earth: Countdown To White Day}{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch The penultimate track. Can you believe it's just a couple of days 'til Christmas? I know I can't! }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch This track is dedicated to a friend of mine who, really, I met by pure chance. Some real "right place, right time" type stuff. In the time since we met (dear god, I think it was roughly two years ago!), we've become fairly close. I cop to not having always shown very well how much he means to me (in fact once or twice I know I've been kind of a dick), but the gods honest truth is I value him highly as a friend and a creative partner, and I really should make more of an effort to chat to him. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch This song was done for one of this friend's fan projects- and, in fact, the fan project that actually got us to meet one another in the first place, a MOTHER fangame titled Old Mother Earth. In fact, that's why I picked that course to go down, it seemed the most fitting! The samples from favourite songs of ours (Smokers Outside The Hospital Doors and The Racing Rats by the Editors, Machine Gun by Portishead) are little extra bonuses. I didn't create this to actually be included in OME, and was more inspired by the general tone and direction of the story (or what I know of it, because even after two years I STILL don't know the full story!) and was structured to be like a "Welcome To The Worlds Of OME" type song. The title is also a reference to the Jamiroquai song "Emergency On Planet Earth", more or less because I could. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch Keep going strong, Rec. I know you have your rough days, but I want you to remember that you mean a hell of a lot to many people, and that includes me. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch  }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch 12) That Fat Slim Boy Guy Makes A Rather Daft Discovery: A Micromix For Dio }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch And here we are, the last (OR IS IT?!) track for this year; another short'un (and a micromix at that), but by no means does that mean this track is insignificant. Far from it. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch Well, it had to be done, didn't it? And it pretty much had to be Christmas Eve too, of course. We've been through some crazy times in the four or so years that we've known one another; some good, some bad, some amazing, and all of them worth it. I wouldn't change a single minute of my time spent on this earth since Christmas of 2008, if only because you've been so prominent in my life since that point that it isn't even funny. And I mean that. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch We have our disagreements, but I know one thing we can definitely agree on is Daft Punk (mostly) and Fatboy Slim (completely), so those are the two subjects I picked for this mix. I realise I SHOULD by now know what your favourite tracks by each artist are, so I sampled some of my personal favourites (and, in the case of Fatboy Slim, favourites based on the CDs of his I could actually find). On top of the original material in the track, I sampled Harder, Better, Faster, Stronger, Crescendolls, High Life, and Robot Rock by Daft Punk, and Song For Lindy, Going Out Of My Head, Everybody Needs A 303, Ya Mama, and Weapon Of Choice by Fatboy Slim. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch Thank you, Dio, for being such an integral part of my life that you, for all intents and purposes, basically ARE me. Just American, shorter (hurr hurr), and you don't have annoying dangly bits between your legs. You're my sister, my best friend, and so much more. Here's to another four years of insanity, eh? }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch  }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch BONUS DESCRIPTIONS: }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch  }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch 13) Depechemas  }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch This was actually the first song I attempted for the 12 Tracks project. I dug the concept I was working with, but it not only sounds the weakest compared to the other demos and the final tracks, but even before all the other tracks where completed the thing felt kinda weak and lacking, so I scrapped it pretty quickly. The only element I really think came out ok where the drums, of which only one of the drumloops was 100% custom anyway. Might revisit this one later, but I wouldn\uc1\u8217\'92t hold your breath. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch  }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch 14) Red Field [From "Alley Brawler ZX Gamma"] }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch I am actually a little bummed this one wound up going nowhere in time to be finished for the countdown, because Im fairly proud of what I\uc1\u8217\'92ve got so far (or, at least the first 28 seconds). This one was heavily inspired by the music from the Street Fighter EX games, which I adore (and is arguably the type of music I actually created the Gonkaka alias to make). I still have the master file for this, so I will no doubt be working on it sometime in the future. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch  }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch 15) CHRISTMAS IN THE L.C. YO (or REASONS WHY I'M A BITTER AND DEAD)}{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch Much as I love working with Rotterdam Techno as a genre, I often find it very hard to know where to actually go with it. Thats why there\uc1\u8217\'92s so many Damn That Rotter!!! demos and zero finished tracks. This demo is shaping up fairly ok, but its still a long way off from being done. I still have the masterfile though, so it hasn\uc1\u8217\'92t been scrapped. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch  }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch 16) Hellplace [From "C&C: Hellkiller"] }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch The original concept I went with for the 24ths track; a chiptune-ish track based around Dio\uc1\u8217\'92s Creepy & Crawley series. I was going for something kinda techno or big beat styled, down to using a looped guitar sample. The progression of the song is fairly similar to that of a song from the Konami beat em up Mystic Warriors, semi-intentionally. I ran out of ideas pretty fast with this one, but Ill revisit the concept again in the near future. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch  }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch 17) Coolkid [J-MACHine's '93 Style Mix] [DEMO] }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch The original path I took with the Coolkid remix was honestly not that different from the final version. Some bits are downtuned or uptuned differently because I wound up getting confused (a lot of samples I have are tuned oddly or differently, and I\uc1\u8217\'92ll sometimes need to have other samples tuned in a strange way to get everything matching up correctly). The breakdown that comes at the end was originally supposed to be the middle section, but thats honestly the only real major change between this and the final barring the stripped-down nature of the demo. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch I gotta say, sticking to doing two tracks a day throughout most of December on top of everything else I normally have to do over the Christmas season? Not an easy task, and one that I wasn\uc1\u8217\'92t entirely sure Id be able to manage. But lo and behold, I managed to pull it off; 12 Tracks, each on even numbered days, never too late and never too early. As per the norm, there\uc1\u8217\'92s definitely some stuff I wish Id done better on these tracks, but this is probably the least intense I\uc1\u8217\'92ve ever felt that feeling of oh, but if I did this I could have etc. etc. This is, without a doubt, some of the best sounding music I have ever put out, and my growth as an artist over this month is incredible. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch  }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch Id like to thank Dez, not only for the moral support throughout this month of sheer insanity (god knows shes probably have an even harder time of it then I have!), but for also doing the absolutely fantastic cover art for me (and for saving my ass in the process by doing it!) You\uc1\u8217\'92re an absolute saint, ya crazy bint. Id like to thank not just my parents and my uncle- who not only gave their usual support, but really took to heart how important this project was to me- but also my extended family, who have also shown support for the project over the month. Seriously, you guys are great, and I could not possibly ask for nicer, funnier people to call my blood relatives (yes Les, even you\uc1\u8217\'92re pretty alright in my book.) }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch  }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch And finally, thanks to all of you dudes over on Tumblr and Soundcloud for putting up with my month-long music spamming. Its been tough, but its all over now. Mostly. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch Sample Origins }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
\pard\plain\ltrpar\ql\s29\sl240\slmult1\itap0{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\abinodiroverride\ltrch NOTE: unfortunately I cannot remember what the sources of certain samples I\uc1\u8217\'92ve used are from (mainly the single-note or videogame SFX samples), and thus those samples go unlisted. Should I rediscover the source/remember the source, and if I use the samples again, I will list them In the future. }{\s29\f0\fs24\lang2057{\*\listtag0}\par}
